@startuml Choose the Language

actor User
actor Browser
participant Frontend

note left of User
  User has a web browser and the address of the page.
  Frontend has a full catalog of text for English and for German.
end note

User -> Frontend: User opens the page of the application.
Browser -> Frontend: Browser sends the list of the preferred languages to Frontend.
Frontend -> Frontend: Frontend selects the first language of the list that has a catalog.
alt The list has no language that has a catalog
Frontend -> Frontend: Frontend selects English.
note right
  Continue to step 3.
end note
end
alt The first language of the list has a region, for example de-CH
Frontend -> Frontend: Frontend uses the first part of the language tag (de) and selects the catalog of this language.
note right
  Continue to step 3.
end note
end
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the page with all text in the selected language and with the choice of the language.
note right
  The button of the selected language shows that it is selected. The name on each button is in its own language: English and Deutsch. The attribute lang of the page and the title of the page have the selected language.
end note
User -> Frontend: User selects the other language with its button.
note right
  Step 4: User can select
  The button English
  The button Deutsch
end note
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User all text of the page in the other language.
note right
  The text changes immediately. The browser does not get the page again and Frontend does not send a new request to Backend. The values that Backend gave stay the same. Only the text and the format of the time of the check change. The attribute lang of the page and the title of the page change too.
end note
alt A section of the page shows an error
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the text for the error code in the other language.
note right
  The trace identifier stays the same. Frontend does not send a new request to Backend.
end note
end
User -> User: User reads the page in the other language.

note left of User
  All text of the page is in the language that User selected.
  The button of the selected language shows that it is selected.
  The time of the check has the format of the selected language.
end note
note left of User
  The page is in English, which is the language for each case that has no catalog.
end note
@enduml
